      "mergeID": "66399b76b6c67f92fc1d7746",
      "mergedPostDetails": "# Concept\n\nAfter joining a group instance of any type (regular, +, or public) a user could be presented with a welcome screen/window/modal of some sort which they have to accept/close, featuring group provided information.\n\n# Motivation\n\nWhen joining a group instance, especially a public or \"+\" one a user might not fully understand the group or a community behind it, its purpose, rules, culture etc. or just the specific event in general. And they might be too lazy to research the group.\n\n# Examples\n\nUser joins a party world group instance:\n\n> Welcome screen pops up describing the event, who's the moderator, rules forbidding certain behaviors or poorly optimized avatars.\n\nUser joins a theater world group instance:\n\n> Welcome screen pops up with the description of what movies are they watching tonight and to avoid lengthy conversations.\n\n# Details\n\nThis could be in a form of a window with text and a button to close it, maybe \"Accept\" it. It could pop up right after joining the instance. It could feature group's description and/or its rules and/or an instance-specific description. It could pop up only once ever per each group, or it could pop up every time with a checkbox to don't show it again. Or it could pop up once each instance. Or if the information has changed.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Add Welcome Screen after joining a group instance",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6476ac2be4f7c649260735a0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a side thought, I wonder if presenting a user with a dialog window that says \"click ok to get kicked from this instance\" would violate the TOS. \n\nPeople got used to ignoring pop-ups. \n\nI do think it's a good idea though.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
